    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A question pad is available beside the pickup desk, and a helper can answer routine questions.\", \"decision\": \"How should quick questions be separated from book collection?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe helper asks waiting readers for routine questions and writes answers on the pad before they reach the pickup desk. Common issues can be settled during the wait rather than at collection.\nStaff finish each book collection before noting any remaining routine question on the pad for the helper. The collection transaction stays short while a separate follow-up remains available.\nReaders write routine questions on the pad, and the helper answers them while staff handle book collection. Questions can be addressed without interrupting each collection."
    }
